{
  "_comment": "P&ID legend recognition rules (io::pid_legend). Compiled in as the default; OCS_PID_LEGEND_RULES=<path> overrides at run time. Colours are RGB. Tag shapes: 9 = digit, ? = capital letter, * = anything from here on (leading * = anything before), other characters literal; tag.shapes adds alternative accepted shapes to tag.shape, and tag.min_chars overrides the global minimum for that class. Distances are paper millimetres; the sheet's units-per-mm is detected from its drawn extent. Circle rules are tried in order; 'inner' is what must be lettered inside ('tag' = capitals + number, 'empty' = nothing), 'inner_is' lists exact values. Unclaimed tag-shaped lettering is sorted into range annotations (XV-0407A～0409A, checked member by member), duplicates (a symbol already carries the value; 'orphans.claimed_elsewhere' keeps them among the orphans instead) and orphans; a tag rule's 'report_orphans' turns the whole listing off for its class, 'report_untagged' says whether the untagged symbols' positions are listed (default: same as report_orphans).",
